=== TITLE: USG Chest (Thoracic & Pleural Spaces Bilateral) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NORMAL BILATERAL CHEST / THORACIC ULTRASOUND STUDY.
- No evidence of pleural effusion, consolidation, or pneumothorax on either side.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: HIGH-RESOLUTION THORACIC ULTRASONOGRAPHY (BILATERAL)

OBSERVATIONS:
- PLEURAL SURFACES: Bilateral pleural lines are smooth, thin, and regular. Normal lung sliding motion (seashore sign on M-mode) visualized bilaterally.
- PLEURAL CAVITIES: No pleural effusion or fluid collection in costophrenic recesses bilaterally.
- LUNG PARENCHYMA: No subpleural consolidation, mass lesion, or abnormal B-lines. A-line pattern dominant.
- DIAPHRAGM: Bilateral hemidiaphragms demonstrate normal smooth contour and good inspiratory excursion.